\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces Experiment E3.6. The constrained policy (seed-0 trained) and the unconstrained baseline re-evaluated under \texttt  {oracle} and \texttt  {noisy} perception (\texttt  {saucepan\_to\_hob}, \texttt  {coworker\_train}; each cell is 60 episodes, 3 evaluation seeds $\times $ 20). The policy's proximity reduction is preserved under realistic noisy, lagged perception (bootstrap CIs across modes overlap: $0.236\,[0.17, 0.30]$ oracle vs.\ $0.198\,[0.14, 0.26]$ noisy), and the baseline shows no oracle--noisy gap because it does not use the channel to avoid. The headline E4.1 table reports the pooled three-trained-seed \texttt  {noisy} numbers.}}{46}{table.caption.38}\protected@file@percent }
